WEBVTT

00:47:56.208 --> 00:48:00.226
and it could make a difference
between the US

00:48:00.250 --> 00:48:03.809
and other places around the world
actually getting the economy going again.

00:48:03.833 --> 00:48:09.351
That's not usual, so this has been
a gift to us today, thank you for that.

00:48:09.375 --> 00:48:10.643
DA: Thank you.

00:48:10.667 --> 00:48:13.268
CA: To everyone listening,
this is an important debate.

00:48:13.292 --> 00:48:14.601
And it's not finished yet,

00:48:14.625 --> 00:48:19.601
there will be many other contributions
to ideas like this, I think.

00:48:19.625 --> 00:48:20.934
DA: That's for sure.

00:48:20.958 --> 00:48:23.184
CA: Yeah, chip in, chip in.

00:48:23.208 --> 00:48:26.768
Thank you all so much
for being part of this today.

00:48:26.792 --> 00:48:28.393
We're back again tomorrow.

00:48:28.417 --> 00:48:30.750
Corey, do you have details on that?